  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Assistance to war-affected population in preparation of winter in de-occupied villages of Kherson region</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Local organisation Save the World has already carried out two assessment missions to the Velyka Oleksandrivka community, Kherson region (1st assessment mission &#x2013; 13.10.2023; 2nd assessment mission &#x2013; 21.10.2023). Velyka Oleksandrivka was occupied by the Russians and de-occupied in October 2022. Save the World expects to be able to help 200 households, approximately 600 beneficiaries, prepare for the winter as part of the project. They are planning to deliver 2.0 tonnes of fuel briquettes to each of the 200 households in the Bilokrynytsia starosta district of the Velyko Oleksandrivska community in Kherson Oblast. The total amount of fuel briquettes they intend to deliver to the affected people is 400 tonnes.</narrative>
  </description>
